    "body": "> Moving the cursor does not fire a select event\r\n\r\nWhy would it?\r\n\r\nAnyway, I think the current spec makes good sense, and I wonder why browsers don't implement it. Anything beyond it seems to require leaving things up to the UA, since we can't mandate what type of input modalities are available; that's very UA and platform dependent. We'd have to say something like \"when the user changes the current selection, or when the user interacts with the control in a way the user agent deems related to selection\", which is not great.",
