    "created_at": "2020-12-10T23:27:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-12-10T23:27:41Z",
    "body": ">I guess in your example you have something selected already?\r\n\r\nIt does not matter really; for example, pressing a left arrow key never fires a select event regardless of whether the previous selection was non-collapsed or not.\r\n\r\n> What is `selectionchange`? I can't find it in HTML or in UI Events.\r\n\r\nAh yes, that one is defined by Selection API spec: https://w3c.github.io/selection-api/#selectionchange-event",
